# .trivyignore — suppressions for the BLOCKING Trivy scans: the filesystem and
# config scans in .github/workflows/ci.yml and the deploy security gate in
# .github/workflows/deploy-aws.yml (severity CRITICAL,HIGH, exit-code 1).
#
# Rules (security audit 2026-09-24 INF-11, plan item P0-16a; enforced by
# scripts/ci/check-trivyignore-hygiene.mjs):
#   - every entry is `<ID> exp:YYYY-MM-DD`. Trivy honours `exp:` itself: on that
#     date the suppression lapses and the finding fails the scan again until a
#     person re-reviews it. At most 180 days out.
#   - every entry names an owner: and a reason: in the comment block above it.
#   - a per-resource property (S3 public-access block, bucket encryption,
#     CloudTrail settings, ...) is never suppressed here for the whole tree; it
#     is fixed, or excepted on the resource with an inline `#trivy:ignore:<ID>`
#     and a reason (docs/evidence/W2/2026-09-24-trivy/ is the precedent).
#   - a dependency entry mirrors a row of docs/security/dependency-risk-ledger.json
#     (the single decision record, enforced for npm audit by
#     scripts/ci/check-dependency-risk.mjs) and expires with it.
#
# Removed 2026-09-25 (P0-16a), each verified against the tree at that date;
# evidence docs/evidence/D6/2026-09-24-p0/P0-16a/:
#   AVD-AWS-0086 / 0087 / 0091 / 0093 (S3 public access block): every bucket in
#     terraform/ (bootstrap tfstate, cloudfront frontend, compliance-evidence,
#     stack vault) has an aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block with all four flags
#     true. The tree-wide ignore only hid the next bucket without one.
#   AVD-AWS-0016 (CloudTrail log-file validation): the one trail,
#     aws_cloudtrail.part11_audit in terraform/modules/compliance-evidence, sets
#     enable_log_file_validation = true.
#   CVE-2026-45829 (chromadb): the pin is gone from every requirements file;
#     `git grep -i chromadb` finds nothing outside documents.
#   GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 (react-router RSC CSRF): react-router and
#     react-router-dom are no longer in package.json or package-lock.json.
#
# Removed 2026-09-26 (W2; evidence docs/evidence/W2/2026-09-26-trivy-inline-ignores/):
#   DS002 (image runs as root): it fired on one file, the vendored skill image
#     .claude/skills/gstack/.github/docker/Dockerfile.ci, which is never built
#     or deployed here. The config scans in ci.yml and deploy-aws.yml now skip
#     that file alone (`skip-files`), so a new Dockerfile running as root
#     anywhere else fails the scan again.
#   2026-10-22 (MR-02): that skip-files entry is gone too. 7df89f4f7 made
#     .claude/skills/gstack a submodule no workflow checks out, so the file is
#     never on disk for the scan and the entry named nothing.

# Removed 2026-11-10 (docs/evidence/L1/2026-11-10-image-size-override/):
#   CVE-2025-71329 / CVE-2025-71330 (image-size, ledger rows GHSA-w3rx-r6r6-pgpr /
#     GHSA-5p2g-fcmc-qvqq): fixed, not suppressed. package.json overrides
#     pptxgenjs's image-size to the patched 2.0.4; the lockfile holds no copy in
#     the vulnerable range (<=2.0.2).

# owner: Security Engineering (formerly dependency-risk-ledger.json row
#   GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm; re-reviewed 2026-11-05, extension approved by the founder)
# 2026-11-06: GitHub WITHDREW GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm on 2026-10-23 ("not a
#   practically exploitable vulnerability"); npm audit no longer reports it, so
#   its ledger row was removed (docs/evidence/L1/2026-11-06-dependency-advisories/).
#   This Trivy entry is kept, unchanged in expiry, only until Trivy's database
#   drops the withdrawn record: delete it then, or let it lapse on 2026-12-05.
# reason: braces CVE-2026-93687 (stack-exhaustion DoS when braces expands a
#   deeply nested PATTERN, CWE-674), vulnerable range <=3.0.3. braces 3.0.3 is
#   the latest release, so no bump remediates it. The only production path was
#   http-proxy-middleware, a declared dependency nothing imported; it was removed
#   (2026-10-05), and `npm ls braces --omit=dev --all` is now empty: the runtime
#   image does not contain braces or micromatch. What remains is dev-only (jest
#   29 > @jest/core > micromatch until 2026-11; now only danger 13 > micromatch), expanding glob
#   patterns from this repository's own config, never from a request. Disposition
#   UNREACHABLE per the ledger. Trivy scans package-lock.json separately from npm
#   audit, so this is the ledger decision mirrored for Trivy, not a second
#   authority. Drop when braces ships a fix above 3.0.3; re-review if a new
#   runtime dependency pulls micromatch or braces.
CVE-2026-93687 exp:2026-12-05

# owner: Security Engineering (dependency-risk-ledger.json row
#   GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5; expires with the ledger, 2026-12-06; reviewed 2026-11-06)
# reason: zod CVE-2023-54404 (array validation accumulates one issue per failing
#   element with no cap: memory exhaustion, CWE-770), vulnerable range <4.6.6.
#   The application copy was FIXED on 2026-11-06 (zod 3.25.76 -> 4.6.7, every
#   server, shared and client import); `npm ls zod --omit=dev --all` lists only
#   zod@4.6.7. The one remaining copy is zod@3.25.58 nested under
#   @figma/code-connect, a design-time devDependency CLI that no script,
#   workflow or Dockerfile stage runs; its latest release (2.1.0) still pins zod
#   3.25.76, so no parent release carries the fix. Disposition UNREACHABLE per
#   the ledger. Trivy scans package-lock.json separately from npm audit, so this
#   is the ledger decision mirrored for Trivy, not a second authority. Drop when
#   @figma/code-connect moves to zod >=4.6.6 or is removed.
CVE-2023-54404 exp:2026-12-06
